<title>JAPAN: Hokkaido Bank rises on news on Hokkaido Takushoku.</title>
<headline>Hokkaido Bank rises on news on Hokkaido Takushoku.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hokkaido Bank Ltd rose on Tuesday morning, supported by the news on Monday that Hokkaido Takushoku Bank Ltd and Barclays Bank had agreed to begin discussions on several areas of cooperation, traders said.</p>
<p>In April, Hokkaido Takushoku, Japan's 10th-largest commercial bank, said it would merge with Hokkaido Bank, the smaller regional bank, in 1998.</p>
<p>At 0035 GMT, Hokkaido Bank's shares were up 17 yen at 158 yen, making the bank the top percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. Turnover was 788,000 shares.</p>
